{:name "judge-intake"
 :purpose "Judge what intake gathered: for each candidate a channel brought in (a commit, a session, a Jira issue, a Slack or Gmail thread), decide whether the vault keeps it as a card, extends a note with it, links it onto a note, or drops it, in the vault's own vocabulary. Each intake tick that has candidates is one attempt, so the kernel judges the judging."
 :executor :agent
 :procedure "Run by projector itself, not by an agent session: the tick (the server's poll at the vault's poll.every within poll.hours, or pj intake by hand) starts the attempt when a channel has candidates and the vault's kernel block is enabled, and src/intake/classify.ts is the judgment. For each candidate the model names one kind (ask, promise, info, area, progress, change, drop) and, for one worth a note, a title, a body, facets and a target; the code maps kind and evidence onto a decision: keep (a card in inbox/), extend (a card pointing at the note it belongs to), link (the owner's own artefact attached to the note that tracks it, no card) or drop (a decline with the model's reason, recorded and reversible). The model proposes, the vocabulary disposes: every facet name and value is checked against the vault's .projector/facets.yaml and an invented one is removed, a merge target must be one of the candidate's mechanical matches, and a candidate the vault already tracks (evidence.linkedTo) only extends or links onto the note that tracks it, or drops, never becoming a note of its own. A candidate with no verdict after two asks is recorded as declined for that reason; a judge that cannot be reached holds the channel and writes nothing. Each candidate examined is one intake/<channel> event in the attempt, keyed by its fingerprint and the source's state, carrying the decision and the reason; a keep or extend is also a proposed intent citing it. The attempt ends done with the tick's counts as its result (seen, created, extending, updates, linked, declined, unanswered, skipped, advanced), or failed when the judge could not be reached."
 :output {:intake/<channel> {:title :string :verdict :string :kind :string :target :string :reason :string}
          :attempt/ended {:result {:seen :int :created :int :extending :int :updates :int :linked :int :declined :int :unanswered :int :skipped :int :advanced :int}}}
 :criterion "Every candidate a tick examined has one intake event in the attempt with a decision and a reason; no proposed facet value is outside the vault's vocabulary; a candidate the vault already tracks is only extended onto, linked onto or dropped, never filed as a new note; a tick whose judge could not be reached wrote nothing and ended failed."
 :trigger {:manual true :started-by "projector's intake tick: the server's poll at the vault's poll.every, within poll.hours, or pj intake by hand; the kernel's tick never fires it"}
 :budget {:minutes 30}}
